    },
    {
      "id": "u-mTngkAFzsUh8iwjGdGd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1964.0666562955357,
      "y": 10651.10890199389,
      "width": 1135.4832763671875,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "iTb5MypN4WKrvTeTTGC33",
      "index": "bH1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 688389737,
      "version": 188,
      "versionNonce": 1832278247,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772674172091,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Asumimos que T es inyectiva => Nu(T) = {0} => dim (Nu(T)) = 0 ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Asumimos que T es inyectiva => Nu(T) = {0} => dim (Nu(T)) = 0 ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3pD-aW872Qhc9jhKaAIhk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2053.8082944791295,
      "y": 10709.60890199389,
      "width": 1001.4000244140625,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "iTb5MypN4WKrvTeTTGC33",
      "index": "bH2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1059061639,
      "version": 310,
      "versionNonce": 1994957831,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772674172091,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Y deberemos llegar a que T es sobreyectiva => Im(T) = V",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Y deberemos llegar a que T es sobreyectiva => Im(T) = V",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4iqsovlzu1OcYOo5crqr8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2049.0666562955357,
      "y": 10801.10890199389,
      "width": 1138.5333251953125,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "iTb5MypN4WKrvTeTTGC33",
      "index": "bH3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2069731783,
      "version": 343,
      "versionNonce": 644123431,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772674172091,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Si T es inyectiva, entonces Nu(T) = {0}, entonces dim Nu(T) = 0\n\nLuego por el Teorema de la Dimensión que nos dice:\n    dim V = dim Nu(T) + dim Im(T)\nCon V espacio vectorial de dimensión finita y T : V -> W una T.L",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Si T es inyectiva, entonces Nu(T) = {0}, entonces dim Nu(T) = 0\n\nLuego por el Teorema de la Dimensión que nos dice:\n    dim V = dim Nu(T) + dim Im(T)\nCon V espacio vectorial de dimensión finita y T : V -> W una T.L",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "u405PE3Upa1oIHKcd4zAU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2034.0666562955357,
      "y": 11081.10890199389,
      "width": 1395.25,
      "height": 405,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "iTb5MypN4WKrvTeTTGC33",
      "index": "bH4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1827291527,
      "version": 522,
      "versionNonce": 1741838909,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773011618962,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Como T es un operador lineal => V = W => V = V, luego\n    dim V = dim Nu(T) + dim Im(T) -> Teorema de la dimensión\n    dim V = 0 + dim Im(T) -> T es inyectiva => Nu(T) = {0}\n    dim V = dim Im(T) -> Por Álgebra\n\nSi dim V = dim Im(T) => V = Im(T) (podrían compartir misma base) SOLO porque\ntratamos con un OPERADOR LINEAL.\n\nLuego como Im(T) = V =>  T es Sobreyectiva",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Como T es un operador lineal => V = W => V = V, luego\n    dim V = dim Nu(T) + dim Im(T) -> Teorema de la dimensión\n    dim V = 0 + dim Im(T) -> T es inyectiva => Nu(T) = {0}\n    dim V = dim Im(T) -> Por Álgebra\n\nSi dim V = dim Im(T) => V = Im(T) (podrían compartir misma base) SOLO porque\ntratamos con un OPERADOR LINEAL.\n\nLuego como Im(T) = V =>  T es Sobreyectiva",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
